# ReadPattern (female only)
# hardware/female/search/read_pattern/__init__.py - started by a female's own Search.setup() (fixed this session; previously Search always crashed before this could ever run live, see SCENARIOS.md 2.1). Stops automatically when Search stops.

0 setup(): no-op - buffers/state (sample_buffer, last_match, etc.) were already initialized at construction
0 whenever this thread is eventually stopped (when Search stops), setdown() is a no-op - not on any fixed schedule of its own, so it's mentioned here rather than after the repeating cycle below
0.01 loop() samples the light sensor as a bool (light_sensor.read_as_bool()) roughly every 0.01s and appends (timestamp, bit) to sample_buffer, trimming anything older than 5.5s (step_duration * (steps+1))
5 buffering continues, tick after tick, until the buffer spans >=5s (step_duration(0.5) * steps(10)) - only then does _try_match() run at all; before that every tick is just another sample appended
0 _try_match() tries 10 sub-step time offsets x 10 circular rotations x every (male, drive) reference pattern, majority-voting each 0.5s bin - on a match (<=1 bit mismatch) it records last_match/last_match_time
0 if matched and detection_cooldown (2s) has elapsed since the last log, logs "Pattern detected: {male} drive={drive}" - repeated identical detections within 2s update last_match but aren't re-logged
0.01 buffering and matching continue indefinitely on every subsequent tick, whether or not that attempt matched - a genuine repeating cycle, not a one-shot check
